 "limitations": [
  "The exposed pad is numbered 9 because the symbol's drain is pins 5-9; neither figure prints a number for it.  Pins 5-8 and 9 are one node, so a different assignment would only relabel copper.",
  "This sheet draws no solder-mask layer.  Each copper region is grown by 0.05 mm, the expansion the project's BSC010N04LS6 land uses; the number comes from that sheet, not from this one.",
  "This sheet draws no courtyard.  The body is the page-9 maximum (E x D1) plus 0.25 mm per side, the project's convention.",
  "The stencil figure is symmetric about the land's outer edges (0.0825 mm inset either side) while the copper is not -- the drain teeth are 0.63 wide and the source pads 0.70 -- so every lead aperture sits 0.0175 mm off its own pad centre.  The sheet's chain is emitted as drawn rather than re-centred, because re-centring would be an unprinted edit.",
  "Silkscreen is not on either figure; only the body outline and a pin-1 wedge are drawn, at project convention.",
  "No 3D model: the package here is 6.10 x 5.00 mm, which matches TI's Q5A, but no vendored STEP exists for it."
 ]
